    "http://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/pecse/": {
      "title": "Professional Experience Coordinator (School of Education)",
      "description": "Professional Experience Coordinator (School of Education) Back to Main Site Professional Experience Coordinator (School of Education) Make a difference in the future of education Are you an organised and proactive professional with a passion for education and building meaningful relationships? Join Alphacrucis University College and play an important role in supporting the professional development of future educators. We are seeking a Professional Experience Coordinator to coordinate mandatory professional experience placements for students enrolled in our School of Education programs. This role is central to ensuring students have access to quality placement opportunities and the support they need to successfully meet their course requirements. Working closely with schools, early childhood centres, university staff and placement supervisors, you will help build and maintain valuable industry partnerships while ensuring placement processes run smoothly and efficiently. About the role Classification and remuneration: This position is classified at HEW Level 5.1 under the Higher Education Industry – General Staff – Award. The position is remunerated above the applicable Award minimum rate. Reporting to the relevant academic leadership within the School of Education, you will coordinate the end-to-end administration of professional experience placements, ensuring students, placement providers and internal stakeholders receive timely and effective support. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinating the sourcing, allocation and confirmation of professional experience placements for students across the School of Education. Building and maintaining positive relationships with schools, early childhood centres, workplace mentors and tertiary supervisors. Managing placement records, student information and documentation within Sonia, the university's professional experience management system. Coordinating administrative processes relating to mentor and tertiary supervisor payments. Liaising with academic leaders and the Director of Professional Experience regarding students with specific placement requirements or support needs. Supporting the development and continuous improvement of placement processes, systems and documentation. Providing administrative and procedural support during student intervention meetings, including maintaining accurate records and coordinating follow-up actions. Monitoring placement requirements, identifying potential compliance risks and escalating matters appropriately. Supporting students to successfully meet their professional experience requirements while maintaining appropriate duty-of-care standards in school and early childhood settings. About you You are a highly organised and detail-oriented professional who enjoys working with people, coordinating multiple priorities and delivering excellent customer service. You are confident communicating with a diverse range of stakeholders and can build positive working relationships with both internal teams and external placement partners. To be successful in this role, you will bring: A bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification (preferred). Previous experience in a tertiary education environment or a relevant administrative coordination role. Experience working with students, schools or early childhood education providers. Strong administration, data management and organisational skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to adapt your communication style to different audiences. A customer-focused approach and a commitment to providing responsive and professional support. Strong attention to detail and the ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines. A collaborative mindset, with the flexibility to support team members and contribute to process improvements. A proactive approach to identifying issues and escalating risks appropriately. Why join Alphacrucis? At Alphacrucis University College, we are committed to developing leaders who make a positive difference in their communities and professions. You will join a collaborative team where your contribution directly supports the development of future educators and strengthens our relationships with the education sector. Essential requirements Applicants must be based in Sydney, NSW. Applicants must hold full working rights in Australia . Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate a genuine commitment to, and respect for, the Christian values, ethos and mission of Alphacrucis University College. Interested? If you are passionate about education, relationship building and delivering high-quality administrative support, we would love to hear from you. Please send your CV and cover letter to careers@ac.edu.au. Applications close: 30 November 2026 Expected commencement: 18 January 2027. Alphacrucis University College is an equal opportunity employer and welcomes applications from suitably qualified candidates who align with our mission and values. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
    },
    "https://ww1.ac.edu.au/job-opportunities/SA/": {
      "title": "School Administrator",
      "description": "School Administrator Back to Main Site School Administrator About the Opportunity Alphacrucis University College (AC) is seeking a highly organised and proactive School Administrator to support the effective administration and delivery of academic programs within the School of Ministry and Theology, Business/Leadership and the School of Law. Reporting to the Faculty Administration Manager, you will play an important role in coordinating academic administration, maintaining operational systems and supporting the day-to-day activities of academic staff across multiple campuses and partner institutions. This is an excellent opportunity for someone with strong administrative capabilities, exceptional attention to detail and an interest in higher education to contribute to the delivery of quality academic programs and a positive student experience. Key Responsibilities In this role, you will: Provide administrative support for the delivery and coordination of academic programs across Diploma, Undergraduate and Postgraduate levels. Assist with the development, coordination and maintenance of annual academic timetables in consultation with Heads of School and Program Directors. Maintain accurate information and oversee data within relevant operational and academic management systems. Coordinate the preparation, review and administration of adjunct academic contracts. Provide administrative and technical support to permanent and adjunct academic staff in the delivery of academic units. Liaise with Registry and Student Support teams to facilitate effective student administration and support processes. Work collaboratively with Teaching Assistants to coordinate course offerings and support the day-to-day operations of the Schools. Contribute to the development, review and continuous improvement of administrative processes and procedures. Participate in relevant administrative meetings and committees as required. About You You are a proactive and service-oriented professional who enjoys working in a collaborative environment. You have strong organisational skills, the ability to manage competing priorities and a genuine commitment to supporting academic staff and students. To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Experience in academic administration or a similar administrative role, preferably within a higher education environment. Familiarity with student management systems and learning management systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Excellent attention to detail and a high level of accuracy in managing information and documentation. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and confidence navigating cloud-based systems. Strong organisational and time management skills, including the ability to manage competing deadlines. A customer-service mindset and a commitment to providing responsive and professional support. A collaborative approach and willingness to contribute positively to a team environment. The ability to work independently, exercise initiative and maintain professionalism under pressure. Qualifications and Experience A completed Bachelor's degree from an Australian or recognised international higher education institution is strongly preferred. Demonstrated experience in academic administration and the use of relevant student and learning management systems. Why Join Alphacrucis? Alphacrucis University College is committed to equipping Christian leaders to make a positive impact in their communities and professions. By joining AC, you will become part of a collaborative and mission-driven environment where your contribution supports the delivery of quality higher education and the development of future leaders. Our Mission and Values As a Christian higher education institution, Alphacrucis University College welcomes applicants who can support and contribute positively to its Christian ethos, mission and values. How to Apply If you are an organised and collaborative administrator who is passionate about supporting higher education, we encourage you to apply. Please submit your application, including your resume and a cover letter outlining your suitability for the role, and send it to careers@ac.edu.au. Note: Only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. Alphacrucis University College Ltd | ABN: 13072747187 RTO: 90525 | TEQSA: PRV12006 ‘University College’ | CRICOS: 00958A"
